course: dictionary
lesson: 8409
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, so do not stop at the first one you know. Read the words around it and ask which meaning fits. This is context at work.
explain: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» Here run means to move fast on your feet. The danger words and slippery floors are the clues: a fast move is what they warn about.
explain: «The Mole's thoughts ran a good deal on supper.» Thoughts cannot move on feet, so run must mean something else. Try swapping in move fast: it makes no sense. Always test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Run is a verb and a noun: run, runs, ran, running, and a run.
fact: To run means to move fast on your feet.
fact: A run is a time of running, like a morning run.
fact: To run out (of) means to have none left.
fact: In cricket and baseball, a run is a point scored. In maths, speed = distance ÷ time.
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» What does run mean in this sentence? | *To move fast on your feet | A point scored in cricket | Water flowing out of a tap | To manage a club
exercise: In cricket, what is a run? | A fast trip to the shops | *A point scored | A boat race | A row of good luck
exercise: Maya says, «My nose runs when I have a cold.» What does runs mean here? | *Liquid flows out | To manage a business | To score a point | To move fast on her feet
test: «The bus runs every 10 minutes.» What does runs mean here? | It is the end of a race | It flows out like water | *It travels on a route | It moves fast on its wheels like a runner
test: «I have run out of time.» What does run out of mean? | To go outside quickly | To win a race | To flow like water | *To have none left
exam: Which word is the formal, stiff word for run, as in «the service ___ every 15 minutes»? | jumps | sings | *operates | hides
